│ patch_description        │ The validation failure was caused by the original implementation corrupting row placement │
│                          │ and column identity during recursive processing. In particular, `column_recursion` wrote  │
│                          │ completed futures back using enumeration order rather than the source row index,          │
│                          │ `original_index` was added and later used as a data column, recursive DataFrame           │
│                          │ reconstruction discarded labels/types, and the method returned an empty column-ordering   │
│                          │ list despite changing row contents. The implementation also optimized cell-level          │
│                          │ statistics rather than the serialized character-prefix objective.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This replacement preserves every original row, value, shape, index, and column label. It  │
│                          │ constructs a small bounded set of column-order candidates, scores each candidate using    │
│                          │ the exact sorted serialized-row LCP objective, selects the best one, lexicographically    │
│                          │ orders the resulting strings, and returns valid per-row column orderings. It avoids       │
│                          │ modifying cells for scoring and handles missing and mixed values through a separate       │
│                          │ serialization representation.                                                             │
