│ patch_description        │ The previous implementation could corrupt row identity and cell placement: it added an    │
│                          │ `original_index` cell, rebuilt frames from raw `.values`, wrote threaded results using    │
│                          │ completion order rather than source row order, merged/re-sorted data, and finally         │
│                          │ returned an empty `column_orderings` list. These behaviors violate the required           │
│                          │ preservation and row-specific ordering contract. The stdout only shows the algorithm      │
│                          │ reached preprocessing; no useful traceback was emitted, so the validation failure is      │
│                          │ consistent with these structural correctness issues.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This replacement preserves every original cell and row index, never adds helper columns,  │
│                          │ handles missing and mixed values safely, and returns a valid column ordering for every    │
│                          │ row. It evaluates a bounded set of column-order candidates using exact serialized-row     │
│                          │ Trie reuse via sorted-string LCP scoring, selecting between frequency-based global orders │
│                          │ and a bounded conditional grouping order.                                                 │
