│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ trie_safe_reorder                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The original implementation could corrupt rows and columns during recursive               │
│                          │ reconstruction: it created new DataFrames from value lists, used asynchronous completion  │
│                          │ order as row order, merged on a synthetic index, dropped/recreated columns, and finally   │
│                          │ returned an empty column-ordering list. This violates the required API because            │
│                          │ row-specific permutations cannot be interpreted without valid per-row orderings, and      │
│                          │ mixed/missing values may be altered by pandas reconstruction.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement preserves every original value, row, index, and shape. It builds a small  │
│                          │ bounded set of column-order candidates, measures their actual serialized Trie-prefix      │
│                          │ reuse using sorted-string LCP scoring, and returns the best candidate together with valid │
│                          │ per-row column orderings. It supports mixed values and missing values without changing    │
│                          │ stored data, honors merge/dependency ordering constraints, and avoids the unsafe          │
│                          │ recursive DataFrame mutation paths.                                                       │
