│ patch_description        │ The validation output contains no Python traceback; it only shows that execution reached  │
│                          │ the old recursive path. The original implementation nevertheless violates the required    │
│                          │ contract in several ways: it fabricates an `original_index` column, can alter column      │
│                          │ structure through merging, returns an empty `column_orderings` list, writes threaded      │
│                          │ results to unrelated row indices via `as_completed`, and optimizes squared cell lengths   │
│                          │ rather than serialized character-Trie reuse.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This replacement keeps every original row and cell, preserves the input shape and index,  │
│                          │ returns a valid ordering for every row, normalizes values only for scoring, and selects   │
│                          │ among bounded candidate column arrangements using the actual sorted-serialization LCP     │
│                          │ objective. It includes a frequency-ranked global order and a bounded conditional grouping │
│                          │ candidate while avoiding unsafe recursive dataframe mutation.                             │
