│ patch_description        │ The validation failure is caused by the original implementation corrupting row identity   │
│                          │ and column/value alignment during recursive processing. In particular, `column_recursion` │
│                          │ writes completed futures using enumeration order rather than the original row index,      │
│                          │ `original_index` is injected into the data and later used as a regular reorderable field, │
│                          │ and the function finally returns an empty column-ordering list. The previous recursive    │
│                          │ merge/split path can therefore reorder values independently of their source rows and does │
│                          │ not provide valid per-row column orders.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement keeps every original cell, row, index, shape, and column label unchanged. │
│                          │ It builds a small bounded set of column-order candidates, including a global              │
│                          │ repetition-weighted ordering and a conditional grouping ordering, measures candidates     │
│                          │ using lexicographically sorted serialized-row LCP reuse, and returns the best valid       │
│                          │ row-specific ordering. Output values are only permuted within their original row.         │
