│ patch_description        │ The original implementation was invalid because it could corrupt row identity and cell    │
│                          │ placement: `as_completed()` results were written using completion order rather than the   │
│                          │ source row index, recursive reconstruction discarded indexes and rebuilt frames from raw  │
│                          │ values, and the code added/removes an `original_index` column while also attempting       │
│                          │ column merging and sorting. It also returned an empty column-ordering list, which is      │
│                          │ invalid for row-specific column permutations.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement preserves every row and cell value, never fabricates helper columns,      │
│                          │ supports mixed values and missing values, returns a valid ordering for every row, and     │
│                          │ selects between bounded prompt-prefix candidates using the actual serialized character    │
│                          │ Trie objective (sorted-string LCP sum). It includes a global frequency-ranked ordering, a │
│                          │ conditional grouping ordering, and a second cheap global alternative.                     │
